Rules of Exception Law

1. Logic Puzzle, "For every exception there is an exception, except the exception.".

2. How exception theory came to be, "It started with 'For every exception there is and exception.'. Which then logically led to 'except the exception'. Then came a question; how many of those "except the exception"'s 'exception' are there? It was a hard thing to figure out and crack. Then, Exception Theory became what you see. It was all derived from that.

3. P is for Point, it is the substrate. A Point is infinite. An unbound point is infinite. P is bound to D. The ultimate Point is the total set of infinities, Absolute Infinity.

4. D is for Descriptor, a descriptor describes a point. A Descriptor is Finite. There are finite ways to describe a Point. D is bound to P. An unbound Descriptor would be infinite. However, D is always bound to P, and this binding makes D finite - there are finite ways to describe any given Point. The infinite potential of unbound D explains why D can describe any Point across the infinite set of P, but once bound, D becomes finite. The ultimate Descriptor is the total set of finite, Absolute Finite.

5. T is for Traverser, it traverses. A Traverser is Indeterminate. A Traverser can traverse any number of (P°D) as it is indeterminate. There is no limit to the number of T bound at a (P°D) because it is indeterminate. Examples are consciousness, entanglement, and gravity. T binds to D. T is limited by the descriptors it binds to, not all T bind to all D due to indeterminacy. T does not bind to P. T binds anywhere in (P°D) as they are bound. T travels P by using D as (P°D) are bound. The ultimate Traverser is the total set of indeterminate, Absolute Indeterminate.

6. The binding and interaction are the same. Binding/Interaction is inherent and intrinsic. There is only an illusion that Binding/Interaction is weaker or stronger. T does not collapse into a singularity with (P°D) because it is indeterminate. We will call this Mediation (Binding/Interaction).

7. The Binding/Interaction of PD or PDT is what makes something Substantiated (Moment/Exception) or Unsubstantiated (Potential). Pure (P°D) is Unsubstantiated. (P°D) with T is Substantiated, this moment is the Exception. This is the equivalent of mathematical nothing, not 0.

8. The Exception is the grounding factor of Exception Theory. Anything and Everything is possible, except the exception. The Exception/Moment is the grounding thing that is impossible as interaction only traverses to other (P°D) when an outside force acts on it.

9. 'Something' and its parts, everything and anything, is relational. There is only pure relativism.

10. S is for 'Something'. 'Something' is everything and anything. 'Something' is comprised of PDT. PDT generates 'Something'. Outside of 'Something' is still 'Something'.

11. S = (P°D°T)

12. (P°D)°T or T°(P°D) as the T placement does not matter due to (P°D) Binding/Interaction. There can never be (D°P) as a Descriptor must describe a Point.

13. "True" Absolute Nothing cannot exist. The moment it can have a name or be described means it can be described and thus it is 'Something'. One can only attach 'Something' to it, this leads to there always being 'Something'.

14. There is grounding or there is prosperity.

15. E is for Exception.

16. I is for Incoherence. Incoherence coincides with the Exception. They are the prohibited and self-defeating things.

17. M (B/I) is for Mediation (Binding/Interaction).

18. PDT = EIM so 3=3.

19. More D can be found using other D.

20. Regions that are True Exception or Incoherent are unable to be traversed. The Moment is complete and any interaction traverses to another. Incoherence has no traverser but cannot be traversed to. They would be noticeable for their unnoticeability. They cover both configuration of Substantiated and Unsubstantiated.


























